  "abstract": "Ihō naigaishū is a manuscript collection of medical prescriptions held in the Fujikawa Collection at Kyoto University (RB00001162). It records historical medical conditions, ingredients, and quantities in entries for decoctions, pills, and topical preparations. Katakana appears alongside literary Chinese, with more extended Japanese passages near the end. Some opening prescriptions also appear in Waike zhengzong. The manuscript preserves its own sequence, abridgments, and mixed writing, offering material for studying Japanese prescription collections and the transmission of Chinese medical knowledge. The dataset maps to 44 official images, including 39 images bearing the main text, and provides JSON, TXT, TEI, and an item-level review ledger. The AI-reviewed edition records 272 unresolved comparison items in the primary review. Full human collation is outstanding.",
